Evening sweep November 6 2026, fired on the 21:00 MST tick ten hours after the midday supplement, and the canonical moved for the first time in four passes. The mcpservers.org twelve-sitemap canonical returned 19,859 server URLs against 19,733 at the 04:32 capture, 126 additions and zero removals, from 29,197 raw URLs across 15 documents with the locale prefixes stripped before the diff and the /servers/ subset taken as the universe, because static.xml now carries the marketing surface and a naive union over-reports by roughly 9,300 URLs. One addition is a duplicate of our own tail rather than a server: /servers/corpusiq/corpusiq-docs is the documentation repository listed as its own entry beside /servers/corpusiq-io. mcpservers.org /all answered 403 for the sixth consecutive pass and every detail page with it, a standing condition rather than an incident. The mcp.so homepage parsed to 132 card objects across 109 distinct stamps with the newest at 2026-11-07T02:31:44.172Z on both the plain and the cache-busted read, and only two cards sat above the midday-supplement stamp of 2026-11-06T16:54:40.494Z: FIndabis at 00:45:09.004Z and scrapling at 02:31:44.172Z. The submission queue added 16 numbers from 6862 to 6877, every one an arrival. Two servers were catalogued, one from the queue and one from the sitemap only. Basis MCP - https://api.basis1.tech/mcp is remote Streamable HTTP with an npm stdio package, protocol 2025-06-18, registered as tech.basis1/mcp and answering a keyless initialize 200 as basis-mcp 0.0.1 with all 25 tools returned by a keyless tools/list, each carrying its annotations and input schema, while a keyless tools/call answers 401 unauthorized missing or invalid bearer token, so the tier is documented with the schema read live rather than driven. It earns the guide because nothing else in the ledger can check a workbook's arithmetic: an xlsx becomes a typed cell graph, a formula dependency edge list, cell-anchored images and an audit record, the audit recomputes every formula against the value Excel itself cached and reports divergences by coordinate, and the findings name hard-coded plugs found by bytecode-program identity rather than heuristic, broken references with their dependents, circularity with the workbook's iterative-calculation setting taken into account, and links to workbooks that are not there. The vendor's measured corpora are the argument: across the Enron spreadsheets and FUSE from Common Crawl, 4,207 formula-bearing workbooks, 43.2 percent of substantial models at 1,000 formulas or more carry at least one plug, 29.9 percent in the FUSE half and 43.2 percent in the Enron half, and 97.31 percent of 3,344 FUSE workbooks under 1 MB recompute with zero mismatches over 4,033,846 formulas compared. The session model is the pattern to copy: open a workbook as a session, set inputs, recalculate, read outputs, commit, with set_inputs define_variable delete_variable close_session and restore_session carrying destructiveHint. Limits, all stated by the vendor: free during early access with no billing, 1,000 requests 2 GB in and 50,000,000 cells out per key per month, 402 quota_exceeded naming the dimension and X-Basis-Quota-Reset headers, in-memory jobs with a 15-minute TTL, 20 MB per parse, no SLA, and pre-GA status. CarbonMeld MCP - https://carbonmeld.com/api/v1/mcp is JSON-RPC over POST with GET answering 405, 15 read-only tools behind OAuth dynamic client registration or an API key, scope carbonmeld.read. A keyless initialize answers 401 with the body Missing or invalid API key and a WWW-Authenticate header naming https://carbonmeld.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/api/v1/mcp, whose own body confirms the resource, the authorization server, the single scope and header bearer, so the tier is documented rather than driven because every record past the public summary needs a Premium account. It earns the guide because the catalogue could account for carbon and could not buy it: GreenCalculus answers how much a company emits with sourced factors and pinned data versions and the subject stopped there, while CarbonMeld indexes 34,421 projects across 30 registries and 12 marketplaces per its own stats export at 2026-11-07T03:30:28Z, scores them from registry documents under method v2.2 with every rule queryable by id through get_method, and serves search get_project get_projects check_offer corsia_supply get_buyer get_developer get_methodology get_standard get_ranking ccp_tracker my_portfolio what_changed search_articles and get_method. The quota is the operator detail: Premium EUR 9 plus VAT a month or USD 9 for a 30-day crypto payment gives 30 different projects a day and 300 API requests, Pro EUR 49 gives 300 and 1,000, shared across site PDF reports REST and MCP, with 20 offer checks a day, a 120-requests-a-minute burst limit per IP and a 00:00 UTC reset, and the project quota rather than the request quota is what an agent burns, since get_projects spends one project per record returned. Its own boundaries are recorded in the guide: document-based screening rather than verified impact, not investment advice and not certification, a retirement beneficiary is not necessarily the purchaser, CORSIA balances are unretired units of every vintage rather than eligible units, the CCP tracker counts projects under a methodology code rather than labelled credits, no company-level developer score, 16,591 projects queued rather than assessed, withdrawn scores not shown, and method v2.1 assessments kept visible with a rescore_pending status instead of being silently refreshed. Held from the queue with the class named: US Business Verification, state registries for NY CO and CT plus an OFAC SDN screen downloaded per call and a scored match_confidence, on the business-identity and sanctions classes carried by Synorb FinzData SimilarLabs and Velarion and by ScreenVerity QoreNext Trade Screening and Atlas Verified, with the Colorado UCC lien profile named as a capability improvement inside a class with an owner rather than a new class; AdRails at dev.adrails/adrails 0.6.2, Google Ads Local Services Ads and ChatGPT Ads with plan validate-only commit, spending caps the agent cannot edit, human activation and a hash-chained audit log, held behind the approval-gate precedent set by lookfirst which already binds an approval to a call's own arguments with a per-call HMAC, and recorded as a different product from the adrails.ai Shopify revenue-reconciliation server already catalogued under a similar name; LinkJolt as affiliate program operations held on an account-gated surface with no driven session rather than on class; Global Law, 208 jurisdictions and 714 corpora read from local git histories with world_on_date who_wrote compare_dates and provision_history, on the legal class carried by LegalCode and Patsnap with the point-in-time mechanism named as the strongest in that class this month; muster d as agent coordination, PairOnce as a device bridge, CheckMyApp as post-deploy journey testing, CutClip.one on media generation, Schedchie on social scheduling across 13 networks, ChefBear and GAMES.GG as consumer verticals, The Wyze Blog as a UK letting-agent content surface, Highwire and kdraigo on the crypto and trading class, and Agent Field Trip outside operator scope as a public-domain art museum for agents. The 126 sitemap additions were dispositioned in three cohorts plus a remainder: about 20 documentation-mirror slugs reading -docs -docs-mcp -agents -llms-txt or /help/, about 25 marketing pages indexed as servers including GAMES.GG ChefBear Schedchie Purple8 FirstAISearch PropertyIndex Soundlink and Invio with Xero in one path, and eight shunshi-ai servers as one author's fleet under the single-author rule; then Tariffs API behind tariff-monitor-mcp which already stacks MFN 301 and 232 over 19,856 HTS lines, TrackCVE on the vulnerability class, AdSpends on ads intelligence, GapCite on the visibility class with seven owners, KafDesk on developer tooling, Context Engine on agent memory, AI BIM Tool and uCAD on design tooling, Tokfluence on influencer analytics, SyncWith on spreadsheet import, Seqora on database clients, Kanal on WhatsApp commerce, Marian as a pre-launch consumer mortgage, Hea as consumer health, Tulina as an automation platform, GLO case search on legal research and InboxSim as email testing, with Sellfy LoadOptimizer PatentRef Sanctionlistcheck PastCharts Odds-API PuraSIM PepBank Flavo and ManaWG already catalogued or held earlier this week, and Bosco Labs unjudged because its hostname did not resolve. Core listing check: mcpservers.org carries /servers/corpusiq-io in the freshly fetched canonical with the docs repository beside it at /servers/corpusiq/corpusiq-docs, the detail page and /all both answer 403, Glama answers 200 on /mcp/connectors/io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp, mcp.so remains not listed with all four direct slugs at 404, and the official registry holds four active io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp records with 1.0.3 the newest at 2026-10-24T04:07:42Z carrying a 40+ business systems description, which closes the 30+ versus 40+ drift earlier passes carried. Counts: canonical 19,733 to 19,859 with 126 additions and zero removals, mcp.so 132 card objects and 109 distinct stamps with 2 above the baseline, submission queue 16 numbers, 144 candidates evaluated with 2 catalogued and 142 held, guide tree 1,109 directories before this pass and 1,111 after, 1,252 entries counting single-file guides before and 1,254 after, and 3 endpoint probes plus one protected-resource document read.

Midday supplement November 6 2026, fired on the 11:00 MST tick one hour after the midday sweep, and the pass earned its keep on a surface rather than on a wave. mcpservers.org /all answered 200 for the first time in a week and returned its newest 30 slugs, 28 of them unledgered on a first slug pass and 24 never read in this ledger under any spelling, because the page had been answering 403 direct and 401 03 bad IP reputation through the reader proxy on almost every pass since November 4. The twelve-sitemap canonical came back set identical at 19,727 server URLs against the 10:00 capture with all 14 documents fetched fresh and zero additions and zero removals, and the mcp.so homepage put exactly one card above the midday stamp, 2026-11-06T16:54:40.494Z on both the plain and the cache-busted read, while the submission queue added three numbers from #6859 to #6861, ROVE Snow Forecast, ndekoui and Sanctionlistcheck.com, all arrivals. One server was catalogued and it came from the /all cohort rather than the queue or the feed. ZplFlow MCP at https://mcp.zplflow.io/v1/mcp/ is remote Streamable HTTP in stateless mode, 10 MCP tools over an asynchronous conversion engine, API key auth with per-key scopes and token pricing where one standard label is one token, ZPL to PDF at 1 token per page and PDF to ZPL at 3 tokens at 203 DPI and 4 at 300 DPI flat regardless of the output size budget, a free tier of 6,000 tokens with no card and a 30-day full platform trial, then EUR 9 for 15,000 tokens up to EUR 800 for 3,000,000. A keyless initialize answers 401 with error_code UNAUTHORIZED and message missing authorization header and no protected-resource document, because the credential is a static key rather than a browser sign-in, so the tier is documented and not driven. It earns the guide as the first surface here that touches the label stream rather than the business system behind it: 24 programmable ZPL transformers covering add_text, add_barcode, add_qrcode, add_datamatrix, replace_barcode_value, regex_replace, add_timestamp, format_date and the geometric set, which is the layer that makes a PDF from an accounting system acceptable to a Zebra printer and the layer that injects GS1-128 compliance into a barcode an ERP produced without it. The limits are the story the way the write envelope was for Sellfy: conversions travel through the asynchronous engine even though the vendor ships a sub-200ms synchronous REST route because that route is marked not exposed as a public MCP tool, listPipelines and getPipeline are the only pipeline tools so an agent can read the label recipes and cannot rewrite them, upload URLs expire in 15 minutes and results in 1 hour, and dynamic over-budget scaling keeps the line printing while billing overage per 1,000 tokens instead of halting. Four arrivals held with their class named: PatentRef, io.github.patentref/patentref-mcp 0.4.0 over a PatentsView-compatible API for US grants from 1976, held on the patent and IP research class carried by Patsnap and LegalCode with claim trees named in the tagline and absent from the tool list; Sanctionlistcheck.com, com.sanctionlistcheck/sanctionlistcheck 1.0.0 with screen_names over ten official lists at 1 credit per name and 100 free credits, held on the sanctions-screening class owned by ScreenVerity, QoreNext Trade Screening and Atlas Verified where a wider list set is a capability improvement and not a new class; ndekoui keyless with 7 tools over a React component catalogue as developer tooling; and ROVE Snow Forecast, com.rove-ski/snow-forecast 1.0.1 with 9 read-only tools over 667 resorts, a consumer vertical. The 28-slug cohort was dispositioned as one list because the flat sitemap proved none of them was an arrival: backlnk on the technical SEO and GEO class, loadoptimizer and fixragent already catalogued, motionreel revline spritulus viralance and flavo on media generation, merit-legal and ava-fund as prior holds, seller-labs-amazon on the Amazon seller class, changedetection-io on monitoring, countrymanager on app store review data, anylocale on localisation, synchronicity-labs on lipsync and dubbing, statelode as an agent task layer, ryumoon-x402 on x402-paid data tools, ahook on agent webhooks, oreondev on Harbor registry DevOps, yuryev89 on Webex messaging, mselcukozturk as personal fitness, centralcommand-io on crypto perpetuals, firenook-dev on Firebase emulators, switchfrog-com on WebMCP agent detection, helprange on document share analytics, and henokey09 and aptekaonline held thin or single-market. HelpRange and Switchfrog are recorded for the next pass rather than skipped silently: both held on thin public detail rather than on class and both need a driven session when an account is available. Core listing check unchanged: mcpservers.org still carries /servers/corpusiq-io in the canonical while the detail page answers the standing 403, Glama answers 200 on /mcp/connectors/io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp, the official registry holds io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp with 1.0.3 the newest active record, and mcp.so remains not listed with all four direct slugs at 404. Counts: canonical 19,727 against 19,727 with zero additions and zero removals, /all 30 slugs with 28 unledgered on a first pass and 24 never read before, 32 candidates evaluated with one catalogued and 31 held, guide tree 1,108 directories before this pass and 1,109 after, 1,252 entries counting single-file guides before and 1,253 after.

Evening sweep November 5 2026, fired on the 21:00 MST tick ten hours after the late morning read, and the two named surfaces separated cleanly. The mcpservers.org twelve-sitemap canonical returned set-identical to the 11:01 MST capture: 19,513 server URLs after stripping the locale prefixes, zero additions and zero removals, the second exact empty diff in one day and the first time this surface has produced two in the same day. The counting note from the previous pass still holds and still matters: a raw union reads 28,851 URLs and 9,338 of them are marketing, topic and search pages, so only the /servers/ subset of 19,513 is the server universe, and /all answered 403 for the fifth consecutive pass, a standing condition rather than an incident. mcp.so carried the whole window and carried it without the stale-read trap of the previous pass: the plain and cache-busted reads returned the same 172 timestamped cards, parsing to 140 card objects across 117 distinct slugs with the same newest stamp 2026-11-06T02:14:00.852Z, and 13 entries above the late morning stamp of 2026-11-05T17:29:38.960Z reduced to 10 distinct servers once the duplicate renderings were collapsed. The submission queue added 23 items from 6809 to 6831, one a listing update for brewpage-mcp and five a single author's SEO fleet under the single-author rule. Two servers were catalogued, each on a gap rather than a name. Ripplewatch MCP - https://www.ripplewatch.ai/api/mcp is remote Streamable HTTP, registered as ai.ripplewatch/ripplewatch 0.1.0 and active since 2026-10-21T04:13:37Z, OAuth through the vendor's Supabase authorization server with authorization_code and refresh_token grants, dynamic client registration and both S256 and plain advertised for PKCE. A keyless initialize returns 401 with a body reading Authentication required and a WWW-Authenticate header naming its protected-resource document, so the tier is documentation rather than a driven session. It scores ten inputs each from -100 to +100 - hiring, pricing activity, product changes, press and funding, relevance trend, win rate against you, review sentiment, Reddit and Hacker News buzz, plus opt-in GitHub and ad activity - into five labels with below -15 Cooling and above +15 Heating up and a low-confidence marker when the data is thin, and it earns the guide because the three competitive intelligence entries here read only the public web while this one scores that web against the customer's own positioning, ICP and closed deals, fed six ways including a CRM CSV, an email forward address and an assistant reading closed deals from a tool it can already reach. Pricing is 29 dollars a month plus prepaid usage from a 50 dollar balance, first charge 79, no seat fee, refundable within 30 days, with both answers and each tracked competitor drawing from the balance, and the limits recorded are no published tool names, no SOC 2 by the vendor's own statement, business context sent to Anthropic models per request and plain PKCE offered beside S256. LoadOptimizer MCP - https://mcp.loadoptimizer.ai/mcp is remote Streamable HTTP gated by OAuth through the vendor web app, its protected-resource document naming a Supabase authorization server with scope email, a keyless initialize returning 401 with an empty body, and no official registry record on three searches. It is the first load-planning surface in the catalog: the logistics corner held Fitralo for carrier search, HaulierScope for GB operator licences, Container Tracking for shipments and PackIndex for packaging costs, and nothing answered what fits, in what order and what is left over. The assistant checks a request, plans the load, follows it to completion, reports per carrier what fit and what did not, and in Claude and ChatGPT renders the plan as a 3D view inside the conversation with stacking rules as an editable matrix; approval covers the account, full access versus read-only, public share links off unless ticked and which app is asking; and the honest cost is not the free tier but EUR 99.99 a month, because the connector needs a plan that includes API access and API access starts at Pro, against a 10-day full Pro trial with no card. Limits recorded: quota and request rate shared with API keys, actions attributed to the approving user tagged via agent, tool-level analytics with an assistant-written goal description scrubbed of contact details and long numbers, and ChatGPT needing OpenID Connect turned off or the approval page fails. Everything else was held with its class owner named: WisePPC to the Amazon seller and ads entries, Torvex to ad analytics, FlowRunner to n8n, Taskriz to PingRoom, Android Texter to the SMS gateways, Merit Ukrainian Law held because its tool table was not verified this pass, STRG held on a one-line listing and a 401, and Faxbeep, relvectors, Ava Advisor, Motion Reel, post2all, Harbor, Screwtape.ai, VidFare, PepBank, emissaoja, Keysrs, work-access-tools, pagenull, Datacircle, the five CrakSEO submissions, QuotedPart, FixMyPrompt, Holdbird and CorpusFetch held on vertical, thinness or single-author grounds. Core listing check: mcpservers.org still carries /servers/corpusiq-io in the canonical while the detail page answers the same 403 that refuses /all, Glama answers 200 on /mcp/connectors/io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp, the official registry holds io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp 1.0.0 as active with the mcp2.corpusiq.io remote and a 30+ description that stays drift against a 40+ catalog, and mcp.so remains not listed with all four direct slugs at 404 and the paid route declined. Counts: guide tree 1,104 directories before this pass and 1,106 after, 1,247 entries counting single-file guides before and 1,249 after, mcpservers.org canonical 19,513 against 19,513, mcp.so 172 timestamped cards and 140 card objects with the newest at 2026-11-06T02:14:00.852Z on both reads, one registry record resolved and zero on three searches for the load planning vendor, two endpoint probes both 401.

Midday sweep November 2 2026, fired seven hours after the night pass in a window where the delta sat in the submission window rather than the feeds. The mcp.so recentServers block carried 30 cards with a date and the newest at 2026-11-02T14:39:24Z against 2026-11-02T09:04:11Z at the night stamp, so five cards sat above it and all five resolved to covered classes: paperjoy sends handwritten postcards inside Poland, 442ball serves football club power ratings, builders-in-fintech is a fintech news and funding feed, eddyter is an editor integration and forge-by-ui8 is a hosted agent front-end from a design-asset vendor. The mcpservers.org /all page repeated its recorded pattern for a fourth pass, the first fetch returning 18,732 with the previous page of thirty slugs and the second fetch, cache busted with a nanosecond stamp and a different user agent, returning 18,887 with the page turned over, so the read whose counter moves is the live one. The issue window moved furthest, 36 submissions landing on chatmcp/mcpso between #6585 at 04:09:42Z and #6620 at 16:36:30Z, and the whole window was read with bodies in one authenticated call. One arrival was catalogued. Versum MCP - https://versum.suverse.io/mcp is remote Streamable HTTP and keyless for every read, initialize answering HTTP 200 with serverInfo versum-catalog 1.6.0 and tools/list returning all 13 tools in 50,179 bytes, and six tools were called live rather than quoted. list_niches returned the whole index in one object: 128 trades, 5,398 cards and 9,300 businesses, each trade carrying a coverage state and the city zones behind it with the date last passed, restaurant at 783 cards over 1,042 businesses and partial for a printed reason while florist is 183 over 316 and complete. search_catalog for pizza in Tampa answered 12 matches inside 15 miles and handed back a real shelf: Green Bench Brewing Co. at 0.3 miles, its phone number, FOUR CHEESE PIZZA at 12.95 and Pepperoni at 14.50. get_offering returns the price as a claim with the shop's own page as the evidence, price_state confirmed on basis published from semantic_html with the quote field carrying the dollar figure, and it sets availability_state to unknown on basis not published beside it, so what a shop charges and whether it is in stock arrive as two separately labelled facts. find_business with needed_by resolved the timestamp to open_at and returned a task card with state confirmed and the reasoning that the shop is open at 19:00 by its published hours, plus the five cheapest items priced. quote_order answered placed false with reason no_public_cart and said what it had done: the shop's own public cart priced the order in a session of its own which was emptied afterwards, only the delivery address was sent and nothing was kept. It earns a guide because nothing in the catalogue reads a local shop's own shelf, the three neighbours on business identity being GBPly for your own profile, Listings API for publishing out to directories and GoodLeads for new-business filing leads, with Undercart the nearest neighbour and covering online Shopify stores rather than the shop with a Squarespace menu and a phone number. Held: Local Business Facts (Agentric) driven keyless to confidence 0.86 with per-field source and method on every fact and held on class as business enrichment by URL already carried by Vibe Prospecting and Leadbay, with a promotion test recorded for any wanted-by field needing a confidence score; Sumora on the lead-generation class; Evalmee on education authoring; Peerlytics on consumer crypto analytics; Binnacle on developer tooling; Narva and Raywake on saturated media generation; AlphaPrime on the trading and market slice carried by Altair, ValuEdge, fAlpha, BDE and the nine EDGAR surfaces; LetsBot and Perisclaw on the saturated messaging class; Faxend and Tempost each submitted twice inside a two-hour window as a resubmission pattern rather than four arrivals; fixRAgent as already catalogued at the October 14 midday pass; and the Chris Pereira, iMpact and Global Connect Show desks as single vendor or single person promotional surfaces. On /all the unledgered slugs were hologramxyz, whose detail route answers a 404 shell so the listing is real and the page is not published yet, perisclaw-mcp and nova-civai-co-agent-product-admin, with every other slug resolving to an existing guide directory. All five tracked listing surfaces were re-probed because the night pass recorded them as not run: CorpusIQ is live on mcpservers.org at /servers/corpusiq-io, live on Smithery through the registry API at qualifiedName benoit-p/Cprusiq with displayName CorpusIQ while the HTML page route 404s and a control test on two unrelated published servers 404s identically because the web directory migrated to an Arcade-powered directory so every old server route went with it, a recorded migration and not a delisting, live on Glama both as the connector io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp on the newer /mcp/connectors/ route and as CorpusIQ/corpusiq-docs on /mcp/servers/, active in the official registry as io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp with the mcp2.corpusiq.io remote, and still not listed on mcp.so with all four direct slugs at 404. Counts: mcpservers.org /all proxy read 30 slugs with the counter at 18,887 against 18,732 stale, mcp.so recentServers 30 cards with the newest at 2026-11-02T14:39:24Z, issue window #6585 to #6620, guide tree 1,084 server entries before this pass and 1,085 after. Supplement pass an hour later on the 11:00 MST tick, treated as a supplement rather than a second read of the same surfaces: the only new submissions were #6621 Publish MCP, #6622 norc and #6623 Lingard Vocab, all held on covered classes, and one reversal was made with a reason attached. AttriKit MCP was catalogued as the first entry that closes the loop from ad spend to app install to subscription revenue to a budget decision: stdio through npx @attrkit/mcp, published as 2.0.1 on npm with the MIT repository KamyarTaher/attrikit-mcp whose README carries the 39-tool table, get_campaign_decision returning the attribution engine's call verbatim with the vendor stating the model reports rather than recomputes it, record_campaign_decision storing the scale cut or hold call with its inputs, import_spend and pull_network_spend making spend an input, RevenueCat joining purchases renewals and refunds, published delivery scope and renewal_event rules with a Google integration refusing both while Google conversion delivery stays gated on a pending certification, 15 second timeouts on most tools and 120 on the three long calls, a version 1 export cut at the newest 100,000 events, one member per workspace, no web SDK on npm yet, 25 month retention, and the first 10,000 qualified installs free once with no card then 249 dollars a month including 10,000 then 0.015 each pricing 50,000 at 849 and 100,000 at 1,599. The earlier midday pass had grouped AttriKit with developer tooling and mobile attribution and held it, and that hold is reversed on the surface rather than on the vendor because mobile attribution had no catalogued class to be held against, WarpLink having been listed as identified and never written up while Mobzio is marketplace deeplinks for one regional seller set, and because the decision and spend tools are an operator surface rather than a developer one; the evidence tier is stated rather than implied, since the package is stdio only with no hosted endpoint and no tool was called. The five directory cards were re-probed rather than left as grouped holds: 442ball answered a keyless initialize 200 as 442ball 0.1.0 with 12 tools, forge-by-ui8 answered 401 with OAuth protected-resource metadata and fragments read and write scopes, paperjoy-01f7bf answered 401 on paperjoy.co/mcp behind 9 listed tools, eddyter stages a React editor into a codebase, and builders-in-fintech relisted and answered a keyless tools/list with 23 tools in 21,348 bytes where the guide recorded 19, so the guide count and FAQ were corrected in this commit. On /all, hologramxyz/avastudio-mcp answered 401 with 76 tool annotations in its listing snapshot and was held on the ad creative class carried by AdMake and Adspy, and perisclaw-mcp answered 401 and was held on the read-only messaging archive slice carried by Kaption WhatsApp. Counts for the supplement: guide tree 1,085 entries before and 1,086 after. Evening sweep on the 21:00 MST tick, ten hours after the supplement, and the first pass of the day where a surface produced nothing: the mcpservers.org /all newest page returned 18,887 on both reads with the same thirty slugs the supplement had already dispositioned, so the page had not turned over between 11:00 and 21:00 MST and the delta sat entirely on the other two surfaces. The mcp.so recentServers block parsed to 132 raw matches collapsing to 108 distinct cards, newest at 2026-11-03T03:04:06Z with three cards above the supplement stamp of 2026-11-02T14:39:24Z, and the submission window carried 27 submissions between #6624 at 18:15:08Z and #6650 at 03:39:52Z which were read with bodies in one authenticated call; FitCard filed the identical body as #6649 and #6650 twenty-five seconds apart, so the window is 26 distinct arrivals. Four were catalogued and two of them were driven end to end. AICTIONBOT Werkbank MCP at https://www.kulicadvisory.com/mcp is keyless Streamable HTTP, initialize 200 as aictionbot-werkbank 1.2.0, tools/list returning 7 tools and all seven called live: check_price_increase for category C17 paper and packaging with a last agreement of 2024-01 and a requested increase of 12 percent returned market_change_percent 4.8 against an observation to 2026-09, gap_percentage_points 7.2, verdict hoch and counter_offer_max_percent 4.8 with source_updated 2026-10-31; screen_sanctions returned 8 possible matches with list, programme and similarity plus the read date of every list, EU 2026-10-23, UN 2026-10-31, OFAC SDN 2026-10-28, OFAC NS 2026-10-19 and UK 2026-10-30; calculate_notice_deadline on a 2024-04-01 start with a 24 month term, 12 month renewal and 3m notice returned term end 2027-03-31, last notice day 2026-12-31, 58 days remaining and an extension to 2028-03-31; check_discount_window on two open items priced 553.50 EUR of discount expiring inside the window and 146.41 EUR already lost at roughly 37 percent annualised, naming the Tuesday 2026-11-10 payment run against a 2026-11-11 deadline; check_invoice_payment returned verdict stopp with one stop signal when the invoice IBAN differed from the vendor master by one digit, matching the vendor on the VAT ID at similarity 1; check_approval_matrix returned 1 stop and 1 check on a departed approver still named in the matrix with no deputy; list_categories returned 34 NACE categories. Three interface defects are recorded in the guide because driving it found them: the free-text item arrays declare no properties so a people row keyed name read as not in the list while the same row keyed person produced the correct departure stop, language en switches only the summary line and leaves every finding and every structured key in German, and the official registry still shows 1.0.0 against a live 1.2.0. Context Pill MCP at https://contextpill.com/mcp is keyless, initialize 200 as context-pill 0.1.0, 3 tools listed and all three called, each declaring readOnlyHint and idempotentHint: get_latest returned the 2026-11-02 drop on scanner day 18 with 11 checked claims from 10 items and the unverified item excluded, search_claims answered 11 matches out of a ledger of 121 claims, and list_sources returned 20 sources with tier, posterior trust and LB10, Anthropic at 0.799 with a lower bound of 0.63 over 7 resolved re-checks, Latent Space at 0.761 and 0.586 over 8, Google DeepMind at 0.692 over 4, OpenAI at 0.636 over 2, and twelve sources still on the neutral 0.50 prior. Cronitor MCP at https://cronitor.io/mcp answered 401 with WWW-Authenticate Bearer resource_metadata pointing at cron